WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.390
Clocks turn time into events.

2
00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:03.089
Add a Clock.

3
00:00:03.089 --> 00:00:06.412
It ticks in step with the tempo, which the Timeline sets.

4
00:00:06.871 --> 00:00:11.291
Add a Sequencer, and patch the Clock's pulse into its clock input.

5
00:00:11.291 --> 00:00:13.233
Every tick advances one step.

6
00:00:13.686 --> 00:00:15.243
Each step holds a value.

7
00:00:15.243 --> 00:00:19.073
Shape the pattern: a spike on step two, a dip on step four.

8
00:00:19.534 --> 00:00:23.109
Bind the sequencer to Z Push, and the depth steps in rhythm.

9
00:00:23.562 --> 00:00:25.784
Clock divide by N slows a clock down.

10
00:00:25.784 --> 00:00:28.066
Here it passes only every fourth tick.

11
00:00:29.834 --> 00:00:32.846
Trigger to Gate stretches each tick into a gate.

12
00:00:32.846 --> 00:00:36.800
The ADSR envelope turns that gate into a swell and a slow fade.

13
00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:45.655
Send the envelope to Bloom Intensity: the glow swells once a bar.

14
00:00:46.107 --> 00:00:51.029
Probe the envelope to see its shape: attack, decay, sustain, release.

15
00:00:51.482 --> 00:00:52.629
Restore the window.

16
00:00:52.629 --> 00:00:56.311
Stepped depth, and a breathing glow, both locked to the beat.

17
00:00:56.766 --> 00:00:59.640
Change the tempo, and the whole patch follows.

18
00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:01.827
Next: feedback, and a little chaos.
